<article class="env-remark" id="0GL4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GL4">Remark <span data-tag="0GL4">63.5.6</span>.</a> Let $j : U \to X$ be an étale morphism of schemes. Then the trace map $\text{Tr} : j_!j^{-1}K \to K$ of Example <a href="/tag/0GKI" data-tag="0GKI">63.5.5</a> is equal to the counit for the adjunction between $j_!$ and $j^{-1}$. We already used the terminology “trace” for this counit in Étale Cohomology, Section <a href="/tag/03SH" data-tag="03SH">59.66</a>. </p>
</article>